 "doc": "Interface of zrmd/audio/sfxtrim.py (HDA law): the last-mile calibration of ONE fitted sound-effect event. A smooth time-varying EQ (dB per band and STFT frame) is applied to the event's fitted bank chain and optimised by gradient descent on the official perceptual loss (ploss, the quantity the event score is made of) blended with its seed-invariant variant (stochasticWeight, 0.5), so a noise is judged both on its exact cells and on its expected spectrum, against the reference window of the event's own stem. The B1 score (describe.compare, a different set of cues) is never optimised: it is the audit. The gains are stored with the event (fit.trim), so every renderer applies them; only band levels measured on the reference enter, never its samples. FR : EQ temps-frequence lisse par evenement, optimise sur la perte perceptive officielle ; B1 sert d'audit.",
