 "pipeline": {
  "_doc": "14 October 2026: the cook of one event, stages in order. 'spectral' = the shared multi-resolution trim of the music (variant named in spectral.variants), 'eq' = the per-event gradient EQ on the official loss, run on the output of the stage before. Both stages leave the chain untouched; the result is stored baked with the hash of the chain. ['eq'] alone keeps the pre-existing record format (gains only). FR : la cuisson d'un evenement, etapes dans l'ordre. 14 October 2026 (third pass): variant 'full' (the music layouts unchanged, the two guards off) replaced 'fine'. Same official, seed-invariant, critic and audit within 0.1 on Opus, but the B1 audit (never optimised, it carries the pitch cue) is 91.4 against 80.4 after the EQ on Opus and 85.8 against 41.0 on two memo events: the gradient EQ after 'fine' moves the strongest line of a tonal event by up to 970 cents, the 1/12 and 1/18 octave layouts of 'full' keep it. FR : la variante complete, memes layouts que la musique.",
  "stages": [
   "spectral",
   "eq"
  ],
  "variant": "full",
  "eqSteps": null,
  "bake": true,
  "peakGuard": {
   "_doc": "14 October 2026 (third pass): the last stage of the cook. The calibration matches band levels and short-term envelopes, which carry no information about a PEAK, and the cooked effects arrive with a crest factor above the reference window's: of 42 corpus events, 28 peak above the reference, 13 by more than 1 dB, 5 by more than 2 dB, up to 4.2 dB (OneKey E005 at 1.57 of full scale against 0.97 in the reference). The final mix pays that as limiter gain reduction on the music. A look-ahead limiter (lookaheadMs each side, true peak at the oversampling) brings the event peak to the reference window's peak plus marginDb, and touches nothing below. Measured on the 13 events over 1 dB: official score -0.03 on average (worst -0.10), seed-invariant -0.001, B1 -0.1. Only the PEAK LEVEL of the reference window enters (a level, like the band levels), never a sample. FR : un plafond de pic, la crete d'un effet ne depasse plus celle de la reference de plus de marginDb.",
   "enabled": true,
   "marginDb": 1.0,
   "lookaheadMs": 1.5,
   "oversample": 4
  },
  "b1Guard": {
   "_doc": "14 October 2026 (third pass): the guard declared as targets.auditMaxDropB1 and enforced nowhere until now. After the EQ stage, B1 of its output is compared with B1 of its input; a fall of more than maxDropB1 points rejects the EQ (the event ships the shared spectral trim alone) PROVIDED the input passes the headline gate (params gate); otherwise the EQ stays and the report says so. Measured before the guard, official score against B1 on the cascade: memo E001 96.2 with B1 78.6 against 95.6 with B1 99.6 for the spectral trim alone, Opus E007 96.6 with 95.5 against 95.6 with 99.7. FR : le garde-fou B1 de l'EQ, enfin applique.",
   "enabled": true,
   "maxDropB1": 2.0
  }
 },
